[gd_scene load_steps=3 format=3]

; Riftwrought — ROGUELITE I3: LIVE LEVEL-UP EFFECT APPLICATION REVIEW V1 (decision D-295).
;
; One question, asked in play: collect real Experience Motes to exactly the Level 1
; requirement -> the accepted three-card panel opens and holds the world still ->
; one card is chosen -> the expedition's whole temporary build is applied to the
; character before another frame runs -> play resumes with the chosen effect live,
; and the receipt says what is live -> the expedition ends and every value returns
; to its baseline.
;
; IT IS NOT THE PROJECT ENTRYPOINT AND MUST NEVER BECOME ONE. `run/main_scene` is
; still the Prototype App. Launch this scene with Run Current Scene, never Run
; Project, or:
;   godot --path game res://scenes/roguelite/roguelite_live_effect_review.tscn -- --seed 99
;
; IT INHERITS THE ACCEPTED LEVEL-UP CHOICE REVIEW SCENE (I2) AND ADDS NO NODE OF ITS
; OWN. The one line below this header that differs from that scene is the root's
; script, which EXTENDS I2's runtime: the accepted loop, the Experience Mote layer,
; the three-card panel and the receipt all come from the accepted scenes and code,
; neither copied nor edited.
;
; Controls are the accepted core loop's, unchanged. Review keys are PHYSICAL:
;   F8 automatic mote pickup ON/OFF · F6 grid · [ ] camera distance · \ reset
;   F5 abandon the run
; While the level-up panel is open only the card controls answer: arrows / D-pad
; move between cards, Enter / (A) or a left click chooses. There is no close.

[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://scenes/roguelite/roguelite_level_up_choice_review.tscn" id="1_choice_review"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/roguelite/live_effects/roguelite_live_effect_review.gd" id="2_live_effect_review"]

[node name="RogueliteLiveEffectReview" instance=ExtResource("1_choice_review")]
script = ExtResource("2_live_effect_review")
